<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cenwalh of Wessex</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 672</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cenwalh was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wessex">Wessex</a> from about 642 to 672. He repudiated his wife, a sister of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/penda-of-mercia">Penda of Mercia</a>, and was driven into exile by Penda, spending about three years at the court of East Anglia, where he was baptised. After his return he extended West <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxons">Saxon</a> rule westwards and is credited with founding the Old Minster at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/winchester">Winchester</a>.</p></div>
